{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"391ed10661232fda59e19c219e9d19824c9699af8c2a0c943f7173401a065dfb","slug":"cholera-activities2","location":"/subrepos/demography/KoelleCholera/cholera_activities2.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"🛼 Alternative approaches to cholera mitigation","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Daniel Grünbaum","given":"Daniel","family":"Grünbaum"},"name":"Daniel Grünbaum","affiliations":["School of Oceanography, University of Washington"],"id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution Non Commercial Share Alike 4.0 International","CC":true}},"github":"https://github.com/organismal-systems/quant-org-bio","keywords":["models"],"copyright":"2026","affiliations":[{"id":"School of Oceanography, University of Washington","name":"School of Oceanography, University of Washington"}],"numbering":{"title":{"offset":4}},"source_url":"https://github.com/organismal-systems/quant-org-bio/blob/main/subrepos/demography/KoelleCholera/cholera_activities2.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/organismal-systems/quant-org-bio/edit/main/subrepos/demography/KoelleCholera/cholera_activities2.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"cholera_activities2.md","url":"/build/cholera_activities2-89a84951281cee4e7c1321eed3f8ee8d.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cholera mitigation strategy A: Improve sanitation and provide clean drinking water","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"NbRSMimgqU"}],"identifier":"cholera-mitigation-strategy-a-improve-sanitation-and-provide-clean-drinking-water","label":"Cholera mitigation strategy A: Improve sanitation and provide clean drinking water","html_id":"cholera-mitigation-strategy-a-improve-sanitation-and-provide-clean-drinking-water","implicit":true,"key":"S621VNWm2H"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cholera is transmitted largely by exposure to contaminated water.\nAn obvious strategy to mitigate this is to improve access to uncontaminated water, by a combination of supplying clean water sources and improving handling of sewage to reduce cholera bacteria populations in the environment.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"PfhvvPN526"}],"key":"Sn6R5dHImI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"However, this is expensive, and may be only partially successful.\nDepending on the specific infrastructure project, the resulting benefit may be a reduction of the seasonal increases in transmission, a decrease in sensitivity to climatic fluctuations, or a combination of the two.","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"key":"yvQG5k8e7m"}],"key":"y3PMkMOe0a"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suppose that (depending on the amount of money available) investments in infrastructure could decrease exposure to contaminated water by 10%, 25%, or 50%.\nSuppose also that the projects that would reduce seasonal transmission fluctuations are not the same ones that would reduce transmission increases due to climate fluctuations.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"dfl6UVCsXP"}],"key":"lB8CHXulNs"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"That is, resources could be invested entirely to reduce seasonal effects (parameter ","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"V5DQG0aCkt"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"c","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">c</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span></span></span></span>","key":"ArwhGFQ0i3"},{"type":"text","value":"), climate effects (parameter ","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"uUz5HnT3XY"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"b","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">b</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span></span></span></span>","key":"EhTAqH3WR6"},{"type":"text","value":"), or some of each.","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"xYBOhlpclu"}],"key":"YAaOrboxBk"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which approach would have the biggest impact on reducing cholera cases?\nHow does the effect on case load improve with increasing levels of investment?","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"y6TDYQNQJy"}],"key":"WaHPxNgGos"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cholera mitigatio